    "Losses have bounded raw alpha-th moment E|l|^alpha <= sigma^alpha with alpha in (1,2]; the learner does not know alpha or sigma (parameter-free)",
    "Truncated non-negative loss for the optimal arm (Assumption 1)"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "stochastic environments are those with time-homogeneous $\\{\\bm \\nu_t\\}_{t\\in [T]}$ (\\textit{i.e.}, $\\nu_{t,i}=\\nu_{1,i}$ for every $t\\in [T]$ and $i\\in[K]$) ... Assumption 2 (Unique Best Arm): there exists a unique best arm $i^\\ast\\in [K]$ such that $\\Delta_i\\coloneqq \\mu_i - \\mu_{i^\\ast}>0$ for all $i\\ne i^\\ast$."
  }
